    "# BGM CIFAR-10 bridge-family reviewer sweep\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook directly addresses the concern that prior experiments varied coupling more than bridge law. It keeps CIFAR-10, the decoder architecture, training budget, and endpoint samples fixed while comparing:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. straight linear interpolation;\n",
    "2. power schedule \\(s(t)=t^2\\);\n",
    "3. smoothstep \\(s(t)=3t^2-2t^3\\);\n",
    "4. variance-preserving cosine path;\n",
    "5. Brownian terminal-drift bridges at three noise scales;\n",
    "6. a variance-exploding corruption path.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same pre-training PCA/\\(k\\)-NN proxy, endpoint cost, target variance, normalized proxy, and held-out sum-MSE are reported. Correlations are separated into:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **same-endpoint deterministic bridges**;\n",
    "- **Brownian target family**;\n",
    "- **all designs**;\n",
    "- the VE corruption row, which is not interpreted as sharing exactly the same endpoint law.\n",
    "\n",
    "GPU is strongly recommended. The default preset uses three seeds."
   ]
  },
