    "## 2. Bridge definitions and targets\n",
    "\n",
    "For deterministic same-endpoint paths,\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "X_t=(1-s(t))Z+s(t)X,\\qquad\n",
    "U_t=s'(t)(X-Z).\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "\n",
    "Schedules:\n",
    "\n",
    "- linear: \\(s(t)=t\\);\n",
    "- power: \\(s(t)=t^2\\);\n",
    "- smoothstep: \\(s(t)=3t^2-2t^3\\);\n",
    "- VP cosine: \\(X_t=\\cos(\\pi t/2)Z+\\sin(\\pi t/2)X\\).\n",
    "\n",
    "For Brownian bridges,\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "X_t=(1-t)Z+tX+\\varepsilon\\sqrt{t(1-t)}\\Xi,\\qquad\n",
    "U_t=(X-X_t)/(1-t).\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "\n",
    "For the VE corruption row,\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "X_t=X+\\sigma(1-t)Z,\\qquad\n",
    "\\sigma(r)=\\sigma_{\\min}(\\sigma_{\\max}/\\sigma_{\\min})^r,\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "and \\(U_t=\\partial_tX_t\\). This row has a different noisy endpoint law and is reported separately rather than used as a fixed-endpoint causal comparison."
   ]
