    "## Interpretation guardrails\n",
    "\n",
    "The strongest supported statement is target-relative:\n",
    "\n",
    "> Across controlled bridge families, the pre-training proxy ranks the held-out error of a fixed Markov decoder trained to predict each bridge's explicitly defined local target.\n",
    "\n",
    "Do not treat the VE row as a fixed-endpoint ablation. Do not infer that a lower raw proxy necessarily improves scale-normalized predictability; compare \\(\\eta\\) and total target variance. A lower-gap bridge may still generate worse samples because of optimization, discretization, approximation, or numerical stability."
   ]
